      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T07:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This callback behaves somewhat counterintuitively, so can you explain the behaviour here? In particular it sounds like:\n- A call to startTetheredHotspot can only succeed if the SoftAp is idle. If the SoftAp\n  is running or is being disabled, the call will fail.\n- If a call to startTetheredHotspot fails, the callback is immediately called with\n  WIFI_AP_STATE_FAILED and a null interface.\n- If a call to startTetheredHostpot succeeds, the passed-in callback is the only\n  callback that will receive future WIFI_AP_STATE_ENABLED and WIFI_AP_STATE_DISABLED\n  events in the future, until another call to startTetheredHostpot succeeds, at which\n  point the old callback will stop receiving any events.\n- Wifi may decide to restart the hotspot at any time, and if it does so, it will send\n  WIFI_AP_STATE_DISABLED and then either WIFI_AP_STATE_ENABLED or (if restarting\n  fails) WIFI_AP_STATE_FAILED.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1575,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 1575,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8875c14e8ef3f818eb55a3e08b967dde3e19a164",
