      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T01:51:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It turns out a bunch of bad things happen in Wifi if this happens.\n\n1) The new request\u0027s SoftApCallback will overwrite the old listener.\n2) The restart CMD_SET_AP will run, SoftApManager(1) will be started, and the new listener will get WIFI_AP_STATE_ENABLED\n3) The new request\u0027s CMD_SET_AP will run, SoftApManager(2) will fail due to no interface available, and the new request\u0027s SoftApCallback will get WIFI_AP_STATE_FAILED\n3) Even though we got WIFI_AP_STATE_FAILED (from SoftApManager(2)), SoftApManager(1) will still be active.\n\nI\u0027ve spun-off a bug at b/403164072 to track this.",
      "parentUuid": "470cb82a_8c787782",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1593,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 1593,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "8875c14e8ef3f818eb55a3e08b967dde3e19a164",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
